"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThrough the dramatic device of a murder case, it shows the moral and emotional collapse of a seemingly ordinary family.  \nThe mystery in this work seems to be not  but how was this tragedy possible.  \n\nIn this work, the culprit of the case is revealed at the beginning, intentionally showing that the author's core question is not .  \n\nUnder the name of family, it depicts a cold situation where the most vulnerable member is sacrificed to protect the monster they created.  \n\nThrough the work, the author seems to offer sharp criticism regarding the collapse of extended families, the problem of elderly alienation, and the absence of parental guidance."